  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1046 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nTo start next week, it does look like we might see more influence \nfrom the Bermuda Ridge. This means yes, we could see a few storms, \nbut temps and heat indexes will probably be the warmest of this \nforecast package Monday and Tuesday. Right now, I don't anticipate \nany heat headlines, but the heat and humidity should be cranking. \nFor the time being, models are in pretty good agreement in the \nextended part of the forecast. Temperatures should moderate back \ntowards 90 (maybe a touch cooler) and rain chances become a little \nmore widespread for the second half of next week as a longwave \ntrough takes over the eastern half of the country. So, if your \nnumbers don't get drawn for rain through Tuesday, we all might win \nthe rain lottery for the latter half of next week.",
